60,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Option C is the most logical choice. A bookable system with a shared calendar eliminates the current imbalance of use and provides the structure needed to ensure the room is maintained fairly.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"@Ryuji, while structure is useful, Option C doesn't address the lack of organic connection. However, it does provide a private space for those difficult conversations that currently happen in front of everyone. I find that promising.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,"@Jonathan, private talks are fine, but Option A is the real winner. Think of the time we'd save! No more twenty-five-minute treks for lunch. Let's stop wasting our lives on the sidewalk and bring the food here.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, your passion for lunch is tireless, but let's look at the numbers. We're paying for outside hires for tiny groups. Option C stops that financial leak immediately. It's the only rational choice for the budget.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,"@Shunichi, @May, your needs are both valid, yet we must not forget the silence we all crave. A kitchen brings noise, and meetings bring stress. Option B offers a sanctuary for the soul to breathe.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shunichi"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Servas, a sanctuary is useless if the office remains cluttered with crumbs because there is no designated place to eat. Option C provides a professional boundary that protects the office environment and ensures fair access.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Ryuji, a professional boundary is one thing, but we also need a human one. If we choose Option C, we must ensure it's used not just for formal meetings, but for the honest talks we've been avoiding.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,"@Jonathan, you're still dreaming of heart-to-hearts! Let's be practical: a kitchen is the only option that actually gives us our time back. Why choose a calendar when we could choose convenience?","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, convenience is a luxury; solvency is a necessity. We are paying for external rooms because we lack a professional space. Option C is a strategic investment that pays for itself by cutting those hourly invoices.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Shunichi, solvency is important, but a mind under constant pressure cannot be truly productive. If we only build for the budget, we forget the people. A quiet space allows us to regain the focus we lose in the noise.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Servas, focus is a result of order. Option C's booking system prevents the chaos of ""first come, first served"" and ensures the room is used intentionally. It is the only option that solves the systemic failure of the space.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Ryuji, I agree that intentionality is key. While I value peace, a Quiet Room might only further isolate us. Option C provides the privacy we need for difficult conversations, which is the first step toward true harmony.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, @Jonathan, you're both so obsessed with ""systems"" and ""privacy"" that you're ignoring the clock! A meeting room just gives us a new place to be stressed. A kitchen gives us our lives back. I'm voting for A!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, your commitment to your stomach is almost impressive. But let's be adults: we're bleeding money on outside hires. Option C is the only choice that fixes the budget and the inefficiency. I'm voting for C.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Servas,,"@May, @Shunichi, your desires are clear, but remember that a restless mind cannot find peace in a kitchen or a boardroom. For the sake of our shared tranquility and privacy, I vote for Option B.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Servas, tranquility cannot exist in a state of disorder. Option C is the only choice that replaces chaos with a fair, transparent system of accountability. For the sake of reason and efficiency, I vote for Option C.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I have considered all perspectives. While I value the peace of Option B, we cannot ignore the need for a space where we can finally speak honestly and privately. For our growth as a team, I vote for Option C.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,May,,"You guys are so boring! You're choosing a calendar over a sandwich. I'm sticking to my guns—let's stop the walking and start eating. For the sake of our sanity and our schedules, I vote for Option A!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"It's clear the majority has already woken up to the reality of the situation. We can't keep paying for external rooms out of sheer incompetence. For the sake of the budget and basic logic, I vote for Option C.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Servas,,"It is a lesson in life that we rarely agree on the path, yet we must walk together. Though my heart seeks the silence of Option B, I accept the will of the collective.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
